.TH CCOL_ITER_KEY_PTR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_key_ptr \- get a typed const pointer to the current key
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

const KeyT *ccol_iter_key_ptr(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro gives a typed const pointer to the key of the element that the
iterator is currently on.

For a cvec iterator, the key is the index of the element, a size_t.
For a chmap iterator and a cbmap iterator, the key is the real map key.
For a char-pointer key, the macro gives a (char *const *) that points
into the internal storage of the map, and the map owns the string that
the key points to. All other key types come back as a direct typed
pointer.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable that ccol_iter_declare() declares, or an iterator
     inside ccol_for_each().
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
const KeyT* to the current key. Do not free the value through this
pointer, and do not change the value through it.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The pointer stays valid only while the iterator is alive and the
container stays unchanged.
This macro uses a GNU C statement expression, so it needs GCC or Clang.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_iter_val_ptr (3),
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3)
